Verne V0.5 Model License
Version 1.0

This license is an agreement between You and Verne Labs, Inc. ("Verne"). It covers
the Verne V0.5 Materials. If You use, copy, modify, or distribute the Materials, You
accept this license. You also accept this license when You submit an online form
that asks You to accept it, such as the access request form for the Materials. If
You do not accept it, do not use the Materials.

1. Definitions

"Materials" means the Verne V0.5 model weights and parameters, their configuration
files, the source code, scripts, and examples that Verne distributes with them, and
their documentation, as Verne distributes them under this license.

"Derivative" means any work that contains the Materials or a part of them, or that
is made from them. Examples are a fine-tuned model, a modified or merged model, a
quantized or compressed model, and a model trained by distillation from the
Materials.

"Output" means the actions and other results that the Materials or a Derivative
produce.

"Recorded Data" means data that You record while a robot runs the Materials or a
Derivative, such as camera images, robot states, human corrections, and task
outcomes. Recorded Data is not a Derivative. You may use it to train any model. A
model that You train mainly to reproduce the Output of the Materials is a Derivative.

"You" means the person or legal entity that uses the Materials. If You accept this
license for an organization, "You" includes that organization.

"Affiliate" means an entity that controls You, that You control, or that is under
common control with You. "Control" means ownership of more than 50% of the voting
interests of an entity, or the power to direct its management.

"Annual Revenue" means the total gross revenue of You and Your Affiliates, from all
sources, in the most recent completed fiscal year, in US dollars.

"Research Use" means use for non-commercial research, teaching, evaluation, or
benchmarking. It does not include use of the Materials, a Derivative, or their
output in a product or service that You sell, license, or operate for revenue, or
in Your business operations.

"Commercial Use" means any use that is not Research Use.

"Revenue Threshold" means US$5,000,000.

2. License grant

Subject to the terms of this license, Verne grants You a worldwide, non-exclusive,
royalty-free license that lasts until it ends under Section 14 and that You may
transfer only as Section 15(g) permits, under the copyrights and patents of Verne
in the Materials, to use, copy, modify, and distribute the Materials, and to make,
use, and distribute Derivatives.

3. Who may use the Materials free of charge

(a) Research Use. Any person or organization may make Research Use of the
    Materials, at any Annual Revenue.

(b) Commercial Use. You may make Commercial Use of the Materials only if Your Annual
    Revenue is at or below the Revenue Threshold.

(c) Above the Revenue Threshold. If Your Annual Revenue is above the Revenue
    Threshold, this license gives You no right to make Commercial Use. You must
    first get a separate commercial license from Verne. Send requests to
    partnership@vernerobotics.com.

(d) Crossing the Revenue Threshold. If Your Annual Revenue goes above the Revenue
    Threshold while You make Commercial Use, You may continue that use for 90 days.
    In those 90 days, You must get a commercial license from Verne or stop the
    Commercial Use.

(e) End users. A customer that only uses a product or service of Yours that runs
    the Materials or a Derivative, and that does not get the Materials or the
    Derivative separately from that product or service, is an end user. An end
    user needs no license from Verne, and its revenue does not count as Your
    Annual Revenue. Your terms with each end user must require it to obey
    Sections 4 to 6.

4. Trade controls and sanctions

(a) You must obey all export control and sanctions laws that apply to You and to
    the Materials. These include the US Export Administration Regulations (EAR),
    the International Traffic in Arms Regulations (ITAR), and the sanctions
    programs of the US Treasury Office of Foreign Assets Control (OFAC).

(b) You must not use, access, export, re-export, or transfer the Materials or a
    Derivative:

    (i)   in a country or region that is under comprehensive US sanctions or a US
          embargo at the time of the use or transfer, or to a person who normally
          lives in such a country or region;

    (ii)  to or for a person on a US restricted-party list, or to or for an entity
          that such persons own 50% or more of, alone or together. These lists
          include the OFAC Specially Designated Nationals and Blocked Persons
          List, and the Entity List, Denied Persons List, Unverified List, and
          Military End-User List of the US Bureau of Industry and Security; or

    (iii) for an end use that US export law prohibits, or that needs a US license
          that You do not have. These end uses include the design, development,
          production, or use of nuclear, chemical, or biological weapons or
          missiles, and military end uses and end users that US law restricts.

(c) You represent that You are not in a country or region in Section 4(b)(i), and
    that You are not a person or entity in Section 4(b)(ii).

5. Use restrictions

You must not use the Materials or a Derivative to:

(a) design, develop, operate, or control a weapon, or a system whose purpose is to
    injure people or damage property;

(b) injure, harass, or intimidate a person;

(c) do unlawful surveillance of a person;

(d) break any law or regulation that applies to You; or

(e) help another person do any of these.

6. Physical safety

The Materials output actions that can move physical machines. A machine that moves
can injure people and damage property. You are solely responsible for every robot
and system that You control with the Materials or a Derivative. Before You use the
Materials on a physical machine, You must:

(a) assess the risks of the machine, the task, and the workspace;

(b) install safety measures that fit those risks, such as an emergency stop, speed
    and force limits, and guarding; and

(c) supervise the machine while it operates.

7. Distribution

If You distribute the Materials or a Derivative, You must:

(a) give each recipient a copy of this license;

(b) keep the NOTICE file and all copyright and attribution notices in the
    Materials;

(c) state clearly, in each file that You changed, that You changed it;

(d) show the notice "Built with Verne V0.5" in the documentation of the
    Derivative, or in the product or service that uses it; and

(e) make each recipient subject to Sections 3 to 6 of this license. You may add
    terms for Your own changes, but those terms must not remove or weaken the
    restrictions of this license.

An end user under Section 3(e) is not a recipient under this Section.

8. Trademarks

This license gives You no right to use the names, logos, or trademarks of Verne,
except to give the attribution that Section 7 requires. You must not state or
suggest that Verne endorses You, Your Derivative, or Your product.

9. Ownership and output

Verne keeps all rights in the Materials that this license does not expressly grant.
Subject to the rights of Verne in the Materials, You own the changes that You make.
Verne claims no ownership of the Output or of the Recorded Data.

10. Patent claims

If You start a lawsuit or other proceeding that claims that the Materials, or a
part of them, infringe a patent or other intellectual property right, all rights
that this license gives You end on the date that You start it.

11. No warranty

THE MATERIALS ARE PROVIDED "AS IS", WITHOUT WARRANTY OF ANY KIND, EXPRESS OR
IMPLIED, INCLUDING WARRANTIES OF MERCHANTABILITY, FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR
PURPOSE, TITLE, NON-INFRINGEMENT, AND SAFETY. YOU ARE RESPONSIBLE FOR DECIDING
WHETHER IT IS APPROPRIATE TO USE THE MATERIALS, AND YOU ACCEPT ALL RISKS OF THAT
USE.

12. Limitation of liability

TO THE MAXIMUM EXTENT THAT THE LAW ALLOWS, VERNE IS NOT LIABLE TO YOU FOR ANY
DAMAGES THAT COME FROM THIS LICENSE OR FROM THE USE OF THE MATERIALS OR A
DERIVATIVE. THIS INCLUDES DIRECT, INDIRECT, SPECIAL, INCIDENTAL, CONSEQUENTIAL,
AND PUNITIVE DAMAGES, PERSONAL INJURY, PROPERTY DAMAGE, AND LOST PROFITS, EVEN IF
VERNE KNEW THAT SUCH DAMAGES WERE POSSIBLE.

13. Indemnity

You will defend and indemnify Verne against third-party claims that come from Your
products, services, robots, or Derivatives, or from Your breach of this license.
This includes claims of personal injury and property damage. This Section does not
apply to a claim that the unmodified Materials infringe the intellectual property
of a third party.

14. Termination

(a) If You break a term of this license, Verne may send You a notice. If You fix
    the breach within 30 days after the notice, this license continues. If You do
    not, this license ends at the end of the 30 days.

(b) This license ends at once, with no notice, if You break Section 4 or Section 5,
    or if You break a term again after a notice about the same term.

(c) When this license ends, You must stop all use and distribution of the
    Materials and Derivatives, and delete Your copies. Sections 6, 9, and 11 to 15
    stay in effect after the license ends.

15. General

(a) The laws of the State of California, USA, govern this license, without regard
    to conflict-of-law rules. The state and federal courts in San Francisco
    County, California, have exclusive jurisdiction over any dispute about this
    license.

(b) If a court finds a term of this license unenforceable, that term changes only
    as much as necessary to make it enforceable. All other terms stay in effect.

(c) If Verne does not enforce a term, Verne does not waive that term.

(d) This license is the complete agreement between You and Verne about the
    Materials. Where a separate written commercial license from Verne applies,
    that license controls.

(e) Verne may publish new versions of this license. A new version applies only to
    Materials that Verne distributes under that version.

(f) Some parts of the Materials come from third-party projects. The THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES
    file lists them and their licenses. Those parts stay under their own licenses, and
    this license does not limit the rights that those licenses give You.

(g) You may transfer this license to a successor in a merger, an acquisition, or a
    sale of all or most of the business that uses the Materials. You must tell
    Verne about the transfer in writing. The successor must accept this license,
    and Section 3 then applies to the Annual Revenue of the successor.

(h) Verne may ask for information, such as Your name, email address,
    organization, and intended use, before it gives You access to the Materials.
    Verne may use that information to manage this license and to contact You
    about the Materials. The Verne Privacy Notice at
    https://vernerobotics.com/privacy-policy.html describes how Verne processes
    that information. Your answers do not change the terms of this license.
